# goal2/ and goal3/ track only the reproduction inputs -- the probe
# scripts, the analysis reducers and the bench probe patch; the
# measurement cells beside them (logs, times, criterion and harness
# JSONs, gigabytes in the gradbench jsonls' case) are regenerated by
# those scripts per the recipes in nursery-position-findings2.txt,
# whose tables are the record of the numbers.  Two exceptions stay
# tracked: the ReproSmall compiler matrices, whose HEAD column needs a
# built GHC checkout and whose first-session siblings are tracked at
# the top level.  The driver's build tree is likewise rebuildable.
goal2/*
!goal2/*.sh
!goal2/*.py
!goal2/repro-matrix*.txt
goal3/*
!goal3/*.sh
!goal3/*.py
!goal3/*.patch
goal4/*
!goal4/*.sh
!goal4/*.py
!goal4/newform-note.txt
!goal4/ReproV2.hs
dist-newstyle/
